This is at least plausible, but I think it's important to remember
that people do have lots of means of expression that are non-
linguistic. 

>The question remains as to 'why' we go in one direction or another and
>what, if any _one thing_ , gives rise to new impressions within the mind.
>>
>
>>Evolution is the process by which mostly random genetic changes (mutations) 
>>spread in a population because of the advantage produced by the change.

I'd be willing to bet that the genetic changes aren't exactly random--that
genes are more likely to change in some ways than others. (I don't have
a detailed argument for this--it's based on my belief that *nothing*
is evenly distributed.) 
>
